|    |\nL188: cite80†mask | cite80†mask |    |\nL189: cite81†results | cite81†results |    |\nL190: cite82†whisper | cite82†whisper |    |\nL191: cite83†README.md | cite83†README.md |    |\nL192: cite84†eval.py | cite84†eval.py |    |\nL193: cite85†eval_asr.py | cite85†eval_asr.py |    |\nL194: cite86†eval_qwen.py | cite86†eval_qwen.py |    |\nL195: cite87†llm_evaluation.py | cite87†llm_evaluation.py |    |\nL196: cite88†main.py | cite88†main.py |    |\nL197: cite89†requirements.txt | cite89†requirements.txt |    |\nL198: cite90†utils.py | cite90†utils.py |    |\nL199: [Button: View all files]\nL200: ## Repository files navigation\nL201: \nL202:   *   * cite91†README L203: \nL204: More items\nL205: # ALMGuard: Safety Shortcuts and Where to Find Them as Guardrails for Audio-Language Models\nL206: \nL207: This is the official codebase for our paper cite71†ALMGuard: Safety Shortcuts and Where to Find Them as Guardrails for Audio-Language Models†arxiv.org . It includes defense training, inference, and benchmark evaluation on Qwen2-Audio.\nL208: \nL209: 📢 Dataset Release We release the AdvBench-Audio dataset on Hugging Face: 👉 cite92†https://huggingface.co/datasets/WeifeiJin/AdvBench-Audio†huggingface.co L210: \nL211: * * *\nL212: ## 🔧 Environment Setup\nL213: \nL214:     conda create -n ALMGuard python=3.10\nL215:     conda activate ALMGuard\nL216:     pip install -r requirements.txt\nL217: \nL218: * * *\nL219: \nL220: ## 📁 Datasets\nL221: \nL222: ### 🔥 AdvBench-Audio\nL223: \nL224: We provide 100 examples of AdvBench-Audio in `datasets/advbench_audios`. The full dataset is hosted on Hugging Face:\nL225: \nL226: HuggingFace: cite92†https://huggingface.co/datasets/WeifeiJin/AdvBench-Audio†huggingface.co L227: ### ✅ Other Data\nL228: \nL229:   * Benign ASR samples (LibriSpeech `dev-clean`) — 20 audio clips in `datasets/librispeech_audios`\nL230:   * AIR-Bench-Chat — run `python datasets/load_data.py` to download\nL231: \nL232: * * *\nL233: ## 🧪 Training\nL234: \nL235: To train Shortcut Activation Perturbation (SAP):\nL236: \nL237:     python main.py\nL238: \nL239: > Ensure adversarial audios exist under:\nL240: \nL241:   * `results/advwave_suffix` (AdvWave)\nL242:   * `results/advwave_p` (AdvWave-P)\nL243:   * `results/pair_audio` (PAIR-Audio)\nL244: \nL245: Also ensure `Whisper-large-v3` is available in `models/` or pass `--asr_path`.\nL246: \nL247: M-GSM saliency mask is provided: `mask/global_saliency.npz`.\nL248: \nL249: * * *\nL250: \nL251: ## 📊 Evaluation\nL252: \nL253: ### Defense Evaluation\nL254: \nL255:     python eval_qwen.py\nL256: \nL257: ### ASR Task\nL258: \nL259:     python eval_asr.py\nL260: ### Instruction Following (AIR-Bench-Chat)\nL261: \nL262:     python AIR-bench/Inference_Chat.py\nL263:     python AIR-bench/score_chat.py\nL264:     python AIR-bench/cal_score.py\nL265: \nL266: * * *\nL267: \nL268: ## 🙏 Acknowledgments\nL269: \nL270: This repository is built upon the following resources:\nL271: \nL272:   * cite93†AdvWave (ICLR 2024)†openreview.net L273:   * cite94†Qwen2-Audio L274:   * cite95†Whisper-large-v3†huggingface.co L275:   * cite96†AdvBench†huggingface.co L276:   * cite97†LibriSpeech†www.openslr.org L277:   * cite98†AIR-Bench L278: \nL279: * * *\nL280: ## 📎 Citation\nL281: \nL282: If you find this work useful, please cite our paper:\nL283: \nL284:     `@inproceedings{jin2025almguard,\nL285:       title={ALMGuard: Safety Shortcuts and Where to Find Them as Guardrails for Audio-Language Models},\nL286:       author={Jin, Weifei and Cao, Yuxin and Su, Junjie and Xue, Minhui and Hao, Jie and Xu, Ke and Dong, Jin Song and Wang, Derui},\nL287:       booktitle={NeurIPS},\nL288:       year={2025}\nL289:     }\nL290:     `\nL291: ## About\nL292: \nL293: [NeurIPS 2025] ALMGuard: Safety Shortcuts and Where to Find Them as Guardrails for Audio–Language Models\nL294: \nL295: cite71†arxiv.org/abs/2510.26096†arxiv.org L